{"step_index":100,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T08:36:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-15T14:06:26+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-15T14:06:26+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Abhi/AntiGravity/DhanvantariSuite-Phase1-Professional-OPD-v11/DhanvantariSuite-Phase1-Professional-OPD-v11/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 83\nTotal Bytes: 4458\nShowing lines 1 to 83\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \n2: ## Phase 1 Professional Workflow\n3: This build supports both single-doctor clinics and multi-doctor hospitals using one simple UI. See `PROFESSIONAL_PHASE1_VALIDATION.md` for the validated workflow, status model, roles, authorization, vitals, referrals, appointments and billing rules.\n4: \n5: # Dhanvantari Clinic ERP — Phase 1\n6: \n7: ## Product goal\n8: A simple OPD, consultation and billing application that works for both a small single-doctor clinic and a multi-doctor hospital/clinic without changing the user's mental model.\n9: \n10: ## Phase 1 roles\n11: - **Admin**: clinic/user/settings/report visibility; can view billing and all clinic records. Does not edit doctor clinical notes in Phase 1.\n12: - **Doctor**: clinical workflow, patient registration, consultation, prescription, optional vitals and payment collection when permitted.\n13: - **Receptionist**: patient registration, appointments, check-in/queue, optional vitals, billing/payment when permitted.\n14: \n15: No Nurse role, no separate Billing role, no Super Doctor role in Phase 1.\n16: \n17: ## Core workflow rules\n18: ### Single active doctor\n19: - No OPD token is generated.\n20: - Doctor can use **New Patient → Register & Start Consultation**.\n21: - Existing patient uses **Find Patient → History → Start Follow-up**.\n22: - Receptionist can register/check-in a patient; the doctor sees the visit on Today and opens it.\n23: - Billing can be collected by the doctor or receptionist according to permission.\n24: \n25: ### Two or more active doctors\n26: - Doctor assignment is required for Reception/Admin when there is more than one active doctor.\n27: - A daily clinic/branch token is generated for every OPD visit. Tokens are not reused.\n28: - Reception registers/book/checks in the patient; patient appears in the assigned doctor's queue.\n29: - Doctor sees only their own queue.\n30: - Doctor dashboard polls for new checked-in patients and automatically opens the next assigned patient when the doctor is idle. If the doctor is already consulting, the new patient is highlighted in the queue rather than interrupting the current consultation.\n31: \n32: ### Follow-up\n33: - Existing patient must be searched first; duplicate patient registration is blocked.\n34: - Previous consultations are shown as read-only history.\n35: - Starting a follow-up creates a new visit; it never overwrites the old visit.\n36: - Single-doctor: opens consultation directly, no token.\n37: - Multi-doctor: doctor assignment + token + queue/check-in flow.\n38: \n39: ### Vitals\n40: Admin configures who can record vitals: **Doctor / Receptionist / Both**.\n41: - Receptionist records before doctor consultation when configured.\n42: - Doctor can record/update during consultation when configured.\n43: - Latest vitals are automatically shown in consultation; BMI is calculated from weight + height.\n44: \n45: ### Billing\n46: - No Billing role.\n47: - Doctor or Receptionist can collect payment if their permission is enabled; Admin has access.\n48: - Invoice is tied to the visit/appointment.\n49: - Payment status supports Pending, Partial and Paid.\n50: - The collector must be recorded for every payment.\n51: \n52: ## Security/authorization\n53: All protected APIs require a valid JWT. There is no unauthenticated admin fallback.\n54: - Receptionist cannot edit clinical consultation data.\n55: - Doctor can edit only their own assigned consultation.\n56: - Doctor cannot start another doctor's patient.\n57: - Receptionist can check in but cannot start/edit a doctor consultation.\n58: - Admin can administer users/settings and view clinic data.\n59: \n60: ## LAN / hospital prerequisite\n61: For multiple PCs, **do not place SQLite on a shared network folder**. The supported design should be: one clinic/server PC hosts FastAPI + a central database (PostgreSQL recommended for production); reception and doctor PCs use the desktop/web client over the LAN. SQLite remains suitable only for single-PC/local demo use.\n62: \n63: ## Run\n64: ```powershell\n65: python -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n66: python -m uvicorn src.main:app --reload --port 8000\n67: ```\n68: Open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/`.\n69: \n70: Demo users:\n71: - Admin: `admin_user` / `adminpass123`\n72: - Receptionist: `receptionist_user` / `receppass123`\n73: - Doctor: `doctor_user` / `docpass123`\n74: \n75: For multi-doctor verification, Admin → Admin → Add User → create another Doctor.\n76: \n77: ## v8 Smart Simple UI updates\n78: - Today's OPD search added.\n79: - New-patient future appointments supported.\n80: - Vitals are available during new-patient and follow-up flows and are shared with doctor consultation.\n81: - Single-doctor receptionist check-in uses ARRIVED/CHECKED_IN rather than a queue token.\n82: - Multi-doctor token/queue behavior remains automatic.\n83: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":101,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T08:36:26Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Updated README.md with SaaS and DB details","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"# Dhanvantari Clinic ERP — SaaS & Desktop Edition\n\n## Product Goal\nA simple OPD, consultation, and billing application that works seamlessly as both a Multi-Tenant SaaS platform and a Single-Tenant Desktop application. Both models share the exact same codebase, architecture, and PostgreSQL database foundation.\n\n## Roles\n- **Admin**: Clinic/user/settings/report visibility; can view billing and all clinic records. Does not edit clinical notes.\n- **Doctor_All**: Super-user access with permission to view the entire clinic queue across all doctors and manage all modules, including clinical edits for any patient.\n- **Doctor**: Clinical workflow, patient registration, consultation, prescription, optional vitals, and payment collection. Restricted to their own queue.\n- **Receptionist**: Patient registration, appointments, check-in/queue, optional vitals, billing/payment collection.\n\n## Deployment Architecture\n- **Unified Engine**: There are no separate applications for Desktop vs. SaaS. The Desktop version acts as a single-tenant instance (defaulting to `local-clinic`).\n- **Database**: **PostgreSQL is required** for both SaaS and Desktop multi-tenant usage. The schema utilizes composite indexes on `(tenant_id, branch_id)` for high performance logical data isolation.\n\n## Core Workflow Rules\n### Single vs Multi Doctor Routing\n- **Single active doctor**: No OPD token is generated. Registration goes straight to consultation.\n- **Two or more active doctors**: Doctor assignment is required. A daily branch token is generated.\n- **Doctor_All Visibility**: Users with the `DOCTOR_ALL` role bypass queue restrictions and can open any patient assigned to any doctor.\n\n### Vitals & Billing\n- Vitals recording can be configured by the Admin (Doctor, Receptionist, or Both).\n- Billing can be collected by the doctor or receptionist according to their assigned permissions. Payment modes include Pending, Partial, and Paid.\n\n## Security & SaaS Isolation\n- All APIs are protected by JWT. \n- API dependencies (`get_tenant_context`) automatically scope database queries to the user's `tenant_id` and `branch_id`.\n- For desktop standalone usage, a fallback tenant ID of `local-clinic` is injected automatically.\n\n## Running the Application\n### Prerequisites\n- PostgreSQL running locally or in the cloud.\n- Python 3.10+\n\n### Setup\n```powershell\n# Set up database URL (update with your credentials)\n$env:DATABASE_URL=\"postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/clinic_erp\"\n\n# Install dependencies\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# Start the server\npython -m uvicorn src.main:app --reload --port 8000\n```\nOpen `http://127.0.0.1:8000/ui/`.\n\n### Demo Users (automatically seeded on empty DB):\n- Admin: `admin_user` / `adminpass123`\n- Receptionist: `receptionist_user` / `receppass123`\n- Doctor: `doctor_user` / `docpass123`\n","Description":"Updated README to reflect PostgreSQL and SaaS unity","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"c:/Abhi/AntiGravity/DhanvantariSuite-Phase1-Professional-OPD-v11/DhanvantariSuite-Phase1-Professional-OPD-v11/README.md","toolAction":"Updating README","toolSummary":"Update README.md"}}]}
